Round 5 verdicts. Timing: GPU 0 only, serial, flock /tmp/gpu0_timing.lock, s1_sweep.py (reps 3, median).
Gate for every shipped arm: stage-1 h_q / h_s byte-identical to the v5 table in (token, slot) order and
final output rel diff 0 (s1_sweep.py). Percentages are stage-1 time vs the flymoe-v5 table, same run.

== S1-B  pipe=il4 (4 waves 2x2, 256x256 CTA, 128x128/wave, 256 AGPR acc via inline-asm MFMA) ==
iterations (trace-driven, ATT + WaveScope after each):
  1-2  plain schedule: acc split VGPR/AGPR, ~1000 accvgpr moves           -> rejected (register chaos)
  3    half-split operand schedule + asm AGPR MFMA (srcC=0 first step,
       fenced drain)                                                        -> correct, ~= v5
  4-5  DMA spread + mid-step barrier (bar8); WaveScope: bursty DMAs
       stalled 250-315 cyc each on a full TA queue                         -> +1..3%
  6    S1S: LDS-staged epilogue, 16 B h rows + 2 B scale stores            -> +0.5..1.5%
  7    epilogue per row block, 8 chains interleaved (multi-chain DPP max)  -> +3.6 / +4.6% (I=1536 / 384, T=32k)
verdict: SHIP (as the base of S1-C) for T >= 4096. Loses at T <= 2048 (-12..-52%): 256x256 tiles leave
  < 1 CTA per CU (wave quantization); v5 stays there.

== S1-C  persistent il4 (PERS=1) ==
  8    tile loop, prologue of tile w+1 before the epilogue of w            -> = non-persistent (hidden cost found:
       LICM hoisted per-step n_rows offsets / lane math out of the tile loop: 52 SGPR + 52 VGPR spills)
  9    per-tile opaque n_rows (s_opaque)                                    -> spills gone, still ~= (WaveScope: next-
       tile prologue serialised tile-load -> token-load -> DMA, ~2.4k cyc exposed per tile)
  10   next tile's state loaded mid-loop, carried as scf.for iter_args;
       opaque lane/wave                                                     -> +1%
  11   prologue DMAs spread across the epilogue (30 back-to-back DMAs had
       filled the TA queue)                                                 -> +6.2 / +5.9 / +8.7% (T=32k)
  12   epilogue: packed pair SwiGLU (v_pk_*), med3 clamp, bounded e8m0
       (4 ops), 8 B scale writes                                            -> +9.6 / +8.4 / +7.6%
  13   sc2: 2 x 16 B scale DMAs per step per CTA instead of 8 x 4 B         -> +9.7 / +9.7 / +8.6% (T=32k)
                                                                              +8.9 / +7.4 / +6.3% (T=4096)
  T sweep (r5_s1_tsweep.log): T=8192 +11.2 / +10.1 / +8.6%, T=16384 +9.6 / +7.6 / +10.2% (I=1536/768/384)
verdict: SHIP pipe=il4 PERS=1 (default sc2) for stage 1 at T >= 4096, all three widths.
binding limit (trace + knock-outs, I=1536 T=32768): per tile the K loop is 67.4k cycles at 72.9% MFMA duty,
  epilogue + next prologue 17.7k (MFMA idle; VALU/trans-bound at 1 wave/SIMD, cannot overlap MFMA: all 256
  AGPRs hold live accumulators). Knock-outs: no loop DMAs -> -19% s1 time; no B LDS reads -> -2.5%;
  GM=2/4/8 rasterisation (L2 hit 79.5%) -> no change. The loop is bound by the global->LDS DMA path for the
  token-gathered A tile: 16 rows x 64 B per instruction runs at 31-34 B/clk/CU (dma_bw.py), so a K step
  needs ~900 TA cycles vs 1024 MFMA cycles, and in-order issue turns TA back-pressure into MFMA gaps.

rejected / neutral variants (kept as diag flags, off by default):
  r4   extra A/B ring slot so loop DMAs spread over the whole step      -> -0.9 .. +0.1%
  bar5 with r4                                                           -> -1.5 .. -2%
  nopk (scalar SwiGLU)                                                   -> -0.4 .. -5.9% vs packed
  kob / kod / noepi                                                      -> timing knock-outs only (wrong results)
not pursued: 2-K-step A DMAs (8 rows x 128 B, g128dma): +17% on the A path in dma_bw.py (36.5 vs 31.2
  B/clk/CU); would need a 2 x 32 KB A ring and a new swizzle for an estimated few % end to end.

== S2-C  FC epilogue (shared-expert tiles: own row + the token's 4 routed y_rows) ==
iterations (logs: r5_s2c_fcb.log, r5_s2c_fcb2.log; traces att_r5/s2fcb):
  1    v5 trace (I=1536 T=32k, fused launch): 79k-cycle epilogue per wave, serial tok -> inv -> row
       chain per 8 rows. FCB: batched epilogue (all token ids, then all inv slots, routed rows
       prefetched one iteration ahead), same summation order                -> bit-identical to v5 FC;
                                                                               I=768 T=32k +9.2%, T=16k +6.5%;
                                                                               I=1536 / I=768 T=2k: +-1.4% (noise)
  2    FCB trace: epilogue 79k -> 45.5k cycles but the K loop grew 24.7k -> 45.4k: the hot waits are
       scratch_load reloads of spilled MFMA accumulators (vmcnt(0) behind in-flight gathers, ~1.5k cyc
       each). The fused variant spills (11 old path / 32 FCB) where the rows variant from the same
       template does not: LLVM splits the wpe2 budget 128 arch VGPR / 128 AGPR. agfN (fused launch
       only: amdgpu-agpr-alloc=N)                                            -> agf136: +3.4 / +3.7 / +4.1% s2
                                                                               (I=1536 T=32k / 16k / 8k);
                                                                               I=768: 0.0 .. -0.4% (not used)
       spill count does not predict speed (ag144: 3 spills, rows launch 1.7x slower).
  3    knock-out fcnor (no routed-row loads): fused launch 624 -> 258 us, so the 1.6 GB gather costs
       366 us (~4.4 TB/s). MALL-residency test: per-token cost of the fused launch is flat from T=4096
       (routed rows 200 MB, MALL-sized; also with normal instead of NT y_rows stores) to T=32768:
       19-22 ns/token, gather ~3.8-4.4 TB/s either way                     -> readiness-counter interleave for
                                                                               MALL reuse rejected (no reuse to win)
  4    overlap bound (bench/overlap_probe.py): routed and shared launches concurrently, two streams:
       1638 vs 1598 us back to back; CU-masked split (128 + 128 CUs): alone 1580 / 1038 us, concurrently
       1877 us > sequential 1608 us                                         -> single-launch interleave rejected:
                                                                               the two phases contend, not overlap
  5    shared-launch config free of the routed one (BMF/NWF/DF/pipeF/diagF/GMF): NW=8, D=3, BM=64
       (wpe2/wpe3), async pipe                                              -> all 600-700 us (fused launch):
                                                                               none better than the routed config
  6    ytl: y_rows column-block-major ([N/BN][R][BN]) so a routed tile's store is one contiguous
       64 KB block                                                          -> bit-identical; I=1536 T=32k -19.1%
                                                                               (routed launch 972 -> 1325 us); rejected
verdict: SHIP FCB (default for the fused epilogue; nofcb = old path) and diag agf136 on the I=1536 FC cells
  (T=8192/16384/32768). The readiness-counter interleave is rejected on measurements 3 and 4.
binding limit (I=1536 T=32768, stage 2 = 1549 us with agf136): the y_rows round trip, 1.6 GB written by the
  routed launch (~370 us at ~4.3 TB/s) and 1.6 GB gathered by the shared launch (366 us), runs at HBM rate
  and cannot be overlapped with the GEMM work (probe 4: concurrent phases slow each other). Removing it
  needs non-deterministic atomics or lossy rows, both excluded (lossless, reproducible; rows stay bf16).
  At I=384 the FC path (993 us) stays worse than rows + combine (471 + 453 us).

== S2-D  il4 for stage 2 (256x256 tiles, persistent; with il4 stage 1 writing h_t) ==
setup: il4 stage 1 S1S epilogue writes h K-step-major (HT: h_t[I/128][R][64 B] + step-major h
  scales) -- a CTA's 128 h columns are exactly one stage-2 K step, so the change is store offsets
  only (stage-1 time unchanged: 1522 vs 1526 us, I=1536 T=32k). Stage 2 on il4: contiguous 1 KB
  h_t A DMAs (no token gather), W2 scale block stride KS*256, rows epilogue through a 4 KB
  wave-private LDS row-block transpose (the persistent next-tile prologue keeps the ring).
iterations (logs: r5_s2d_il4.log; traces att_r5/s2il4, s2il4b):
  1    port, bit-identical to v5 (non-persistent and PERS2=1). Trace (I=1536 T=32k, PERS2): K loop
       17.9k cyc/tile at 68.7% MFMA duty (hybrid2 routed launch: 27%), but 16.4k between tiles:
       8 x s_waitcnt vmcnt(0) ~1.2k each in the epilogue                     -> 1146 us for all 5 rows
  2    router weights of all 8 row blocks loaded before the first store (vmcnt counts stores: a
       per-block weight load waited for every earlier store)                 -> 1146 -> 1038 us (5 rows);
                                                                               between tiles 16.4k -> 11.2k
  3    s2tr: MFMA operands swapped (C^T) so an even/odd W2 tile pair is 8 consecutive bf16 per lane:
       direct 16 B stores, no LDS transpose                                  -> bit-identical; -8.6 / -9.0 /
                                                                               -14% (I=1536/768/384): 64 B
                                                                               row pieces vs 256 B; rejected
  4    placement: il4 routed launch + FC shared launch. The shared launch under HT: hybrid2 740 us,
       hybrid BM128 D3 576-593, async 676, async2 677, hybrid BM64 655      -> pipeF=hybrid,BMF=128,DF=3
       serial GPU 0 (s2+cb vs v5 table):
         I=1536 T=32768 +11.1%, T=16384 +10.5%, T=8192 +7.8%, T=4096 -3.8%
         I=768  T=32768 +5.7% (diag2=s2nt), T=16384 +5.1%, T=8192 +2.0%
         il4 rows + combine (no FC): I=1536 T=32k +4.4%, I=768 -5.1%, I=384 -14.3%
         FC il4 at I=384 T=32k: -7.1%
  5    stage-2 il4 pipeline knobs: D2=4, bar4/6/8, r4                          -> all within +-2% (840-856 us
                                                                               routed launch): loop not binding
verdict: SHIP pipe2=il4 PERS2=1 + HT=1 + FC=1 with the shared launch on pipeF=hybrid BMF=128 NWF=4 WMF=1
  DF=3 for I=1536 T >= 8192 and I=768 T >= 16384 (with il4 PERS1=1 stage 1). Not at I=384 or smaller T.
binding limit (I=1536 T=32768, routed launch): per tile the K loop is 17.1k cycles at 72.1% MFMA duty and the
  epilogue + next-prologue wait 11.2k (39%): 256 AGPR reads, 128 bf16 packs, 128 LDS writes, 32 row stores
  per wave (1.4k cycles of store back-pressure). At 1 wave/SIMD with all 256 AGPRs holding accumulators the
  epilogue cannot overlap MFMA. The shared launch (576 us) is the S2-C gather-bound kernel.

== S2-A  stage 2 at mid / small T and I=384 (BM64 wpe3 register split, occupancy, W2 reuse) ==
logs: r5_s2a_i384.log, r5_s2a_sweep.log; trace att_r5/s2a384 (I=384 T=32768, v5 cell)
iterations:
  1    FC shared launch at I=384 (default, hybrid BMF128 DF3, hybrid2 wpe2+agf136)   -> -5.0 .. -13.2% s2+cb
       (T=8192 / 32768): the fused gather costs as much as the standalone combine;   rejected
  2    BM64 hybrid2 wpe3 has 4 spills at K=768/1536 (LLVM agpr 84 / vgpr 168 split). agN (amdgpu-agpr-alloc)
       ag32/48/64: 0 spills, ag80: 5. Serial GPU 0, s2+cb vs v5 table (repeated run):
         I=768  T=256 +7.8% (BM32 NW2 ag32), 512 +8.5%, 1024 +9.0%, 2048 +7.5%, 4096 +4.8% (ag32), 8192 +0.1..0.9%
         I=1536 T=256 +3.8%, 512 +2.6%, 1024 +6.4%, 2048 -3.6%, 4096 -4.4%
         I=384 (K=384, no spills at the default split): -3.2 .. +1.1% everywhere  -> ship where > +1.5%
  3    ATT (I=384 T=32768 v5 cell, 980 waves): prologue 44% / loop 36% / epilogue 20% of wave time, 48 MFMAs
       at 15.9% duty -> latency-bound with 3 waves/SIMD (152-166 VGPR). 4 waves/SIMD arms (<=128 regs):
       BM64 wpe4 (spills) -45%, BM32 NW4 -3..-6%, BM64 WM2 async -0.2..-4.5%, BM64 NW8 WM2 -3.5..-8%,
       BM128 NW8 WM2 async wpe3 +0.8 / -3.4%                                       -> rejected: occupancy not binding
  4    W2 reuse: GM=4 / 16 raster groups +2.5 / -1.0% (T=8192), +0.4 / -0.3% (T=32k); BM128 wpe2 (half the
